98009e4aeb1db06c341c9531956ca" "basis" 2829 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "50cd5ab5d18e05379074b5418ee9130129198009e4aeb1db06c341c9531956ca" "basis" 2829 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+2{t}^{2}\\,k$ at the point $P(2,4,8)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "50cd5ab5d18e05379074b5418ee9130129198009e4aeb1db06c341c9531956ca" "basis" 2829 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,j+y(t)\\,j+z(t)\\,k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(2,4,8)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =2\\,i+4\\,j+8\\,k \\\\ t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+2{t}^{2}\\,k & =2\\,i+4\\,j+8\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}t=2 \\\\ {t}^{2}=4 \\\\ 2{t}^{2}=8.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=2.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, the point $P(2,4,8)$ is at the tip of $r(2).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =i+2t\\,j+4t\\,k \\\\ {r}^{′}(2) & =\\,i+2\\cdot 2\\,j+4\\cdot 2\\,k \\\\  & =i+4\\,j+8\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(2)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{81} \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(2)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(2,4,8):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(2) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(2)}{‖{r}^{′}(2)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot (i+4\\,j+8\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\,i+\\frac{4}{9}\\,j+\\frac{8}{9}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "50cd5ab5d18e05379074b5418ee9130129198009e4aeb1db06c341c9531956ca" "basis" 2829 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b896077b3f61a65625294d246f92b173da2405f8e0fe554beffd6b1050162333" "basis" 2829 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "50cd5ab5d18e05379074b5418ee9130129198009e4aeb1db06c341c9531956ca" "basis" 2829 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{9}\\,i+\\frac{4}{9}\\,j+\\frac{8}{9}\\,k"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "50cd5ab5d18e05379074b5418ee9130129198009e4aeb1db06c341c9531956ca" "basis" 2829 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{9}\\,i+\\frac{8}{9}\\,j+\\frac{4}{9}\\,k"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "50cd5ab5d18e05379074b5418ee9130129198009e4aeb1db06c341c9531956ca" "basis" 2829 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{21}\\,i+\\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{21}\\,j+\\frac{4\\sqrt{21}}{21}\\,k"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "50cd5ab5d18e05379074b5418ee9130129198009e4aeb1db06c341c9531956ca" "basis" 2829 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{69}}{69}\\,i+\\frac{2\\sqrt{69}}{69}\\,j+\\frac{8\\sqrt{69}}{69}\\,k"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "50cd5ab5d18e05379074b5418ee9130129198009e4aeb1db06c341c9531956ca" "basis" 2829 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\,k"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "50cd5ab5d18e05379074b5418ee9130129198009e4aeb1db06c341c9531956ca" "basis" 2829 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{9}\\,i+\\frac{4}{9}\\,j+\\frac{8}{9}\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "50cd5ab5d18e05379074b5418ee9130129198009e4aeb1db06c341c9531956ca" "basis" 2829 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=({t}^{2}-2t)p(t)$ at the point corresponding to $t=1$, given that  $p(1)=i+2\\,j-k\\,$ and $\\,{p}^{′}(1)=2\\,i-\\,j-2\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "50cd5ab5d18e05379074b5418ee9130129198009e4aeb1db06c341c9531956ca" "basis" 2829 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(({t}^{2}-2t)p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2t)\\cdot p(t)+({t}^{2}-2t)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =(2t-2)\\,p(t)+({t}^{2}-2t)\\,{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =(2(1)-2)\\,p(1)+((1)^{2}-2(1))\\,{p}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =0-{p}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =-(2\\,i-\\,j-2\\,k) \\\\  & =-2i+\\,j+2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖r(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(1)^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-2\\,i+j+2k) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{1}{3}\\,j+\\frac{2}{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=1$ is  $T(1)=-\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{1}{3}\\,j+\\frac{2}{3}\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "50cd5ab5d18e05379074b5418ee9130129198009e4aeb1db06c341c9531956ca" "basis" 2829 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b896077b3f61a65625294d246f92b173da2405f8e0fe554beffd6b1050162333" "basis" 2829 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75228" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-